    "https://www.rockhurst.edu/career-services/employer-services": {
      "title": "Employer Services",
      "description": "Employer Services | Rockhurst University Skip to main content Apply Request Info Visit Academics Campus Life Athletics Give Apply Request Info Visit Academics Campus Life Athletics Give Breadcrumb Employer Services Employer Services The relationship you have with Career Development is critical in helping you attract quality candidates for your organization. We offer a variety of resources to assist you with this process.  In addition, please review the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Principles for Professional Practice regarding best practices and professional guidelines for campus recruiting. The Rockhurst Advantage The Jesuit tradition of Rockhurst University focuses on learning, leadership and service in addition to a rigorous core curriculum that is required of every student. This approach produces graduates who are well-rounded individuals, familiar with the Kansas City metro community. Whether you are looking for an accountant or a writer, the programs at Rockhurst University have graduates that fit your needs. Explore the different specialties offered, or learn more about how Career Development can make your recruitment process easier and more effective. Learn More Campus Interviews Employers seeking full-time and internship candidates are invited to visit the Rockhurst University campus to conduct interviews in our facility. You may choose between two types of interview schedules – open or pre-select. Open schedules allow all qualifying candidates to select an interview time without going through a pre-screening process. Pre-select schedules allow the employer to prescreen the resumes of interested, qualifying candidates in order to invite specific students to interview.  To schedule a campus interview date, please contact Mike Theobald, director of Career Development, at 816-501-4861. Employer RU Career Account Career Development utilizes Symplicity as our office management system. By establishing your Employer RU Career Account with Career Development, you can directly post your positions for viewing by Rockhurst University students and alumni. In addition, you can view resumes through the online resume books. To establish your Employer RU Career Account, return to the main Career Development page and click on Employer Partners / Post Opportunities . Exposure on Campus Career Development can work with you to help develop a higher profile for your organization on the Rockhurst University campus. We can set a table for you in high-traffic areas on campus. Recommended hours are between 11 a.m. and 1 p.m. Employers are limited to two (2) visits per semester. Also, we can link you with campus student leaders and organizations. Make a presentation on a career-related topic to a student club or organization, and wrap up with information on your organization. Contact Mike Theobald at 816-501-4861 for more information. Co-ops / Internships The Rockhurst University Cooperative Education Program (Co-op) is a career-related program that allows students to earn academic credit for paid work experiences related to their degree program. Employer Benefits of Cooperative Education Gain access to a wide-ranging pool of highly qualified candidates. Conduct cost-effective “pre-recruitment” without the obligation of a permanent commitment. Increase visibility within the University and enhance college relations. Maintain continuity and reduce turnover costs by utilizing students for multiple work terms. Establish an effective and efficient pipeline of bright and talented employees to fill future staffing needs. If you are interested in coordinating an internship with Career Development, call 816-501-4861 to schedule an appointment. Career Services Center for Career Development Account Setup For Students: Overview Career Exploration Part-Time & Work-Study Jobs Co-ops & Internships Full-Time Careers Career Services Resources Employer Services For Employers: RU Advantage For Alumni: Info & Resources For Faculty & Staff: Resources How Can We Help? Student Success Services The RU Student Success team provides academic advising, tutoring, health resources, financial aid, internships and ultimately landing a great job. (Click for more) Apply Visit Give QUICK LINKS MyRockhurst Portal Calendar Faculty/Staff Directory University Catalogs Photos & Media Jobs @ RU ON CAMPUS Campus Map Library Athletics Bookstore Reserve Event Space Campus Security TAKE ACTION Request Info Admission Process Scholarships & Aid Tutoring Commencement Hire a Hawk CONNECT 1100 Rockhurst Road Kansas City, MO 64110 (816) 501-4000 info@rockhurst.edu Privacy Notice Report An Incident © 2026 Rockhurst University Report An Incident Accessibility Non-Discrimination Standards & Policies"
